## 2026-09-18 (IST) — Failed Upload Management Feature

### Why this work was requested
Upload failures (Cloudinary timeouts, size validation errors, partial multi-file uploads) were being lost on page reload because they were only stored in React component state. The admin had no persistent view of what failed, no way to retry after a session ended, and no audit trail of media upload issues. The request was to build a durable, end-to-end failure tracking, retry, and dismiss system.

### Files created / modified

**Backend — New files**
- `backend/src/main/resources/db/migration/V5__media_upload_failures.sql`
  - Creates `media_upload_failures` table with all required columns and three indexes (listing_id, status, upload_request_id unique partial index).
- `backend/src/main/java/.../exception/MediaUploadException.java`
  - Structured exception carrying `Stage` enum (VALIDATION / CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD / DB_PERSIST), `safeReason` (user-visible), and `diagnostic` (internal-only, never sent to clients).
- `backend/src/main/java/.../entity/MediaUploadFailure.java`
  - JPA entity mapping `media_upload_failures`. Status stored as plain String with enum enforced in service. `internalDiagnostic` never returned in HTTP responses.
- `backend/src/main/java/.../repository/MediaUploadFailureRepository.java`
  - Bounded queries only — no `findAll()`. Includes `countByStatusIn` for badge display.
- `backend/src/main/java/.../service/FailedUploadService.java`
  - Manages full failure lifecycle: `recordFailure`, `markRetrying`, `recordResolution`, `recordRetryFailure`, `dismiss`. `ConcurrentHashMap` L1 cache for O(1) idempotency check. All writes in `REQUIRES_NEW` TX so failure records survive calling transaction rollbacks.
- `backend/src/main/java/.../controller/FailedUploadsController.java`
  - Admin REST API: `GET /api/v1/admin/failed-uploads`, `/count`, `/{id}`, `/{id}/dismiss`, `/{id}/retry`. Concurrent retry guard via `markRetrying`. Retry endpoint accepts optional replacement file.

**Backend — Modified files**
- `backend/src/main/java/.../service/CloudinaryService.java`
  - `validateFile()` now throws `MediaUploadException(VALIDATION, ...)` instead of `IllegalArgumentException`. Upload failures throw `MediaUploadException(CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD, ...)` with a safe user reason and diagnostic. No public API contract change.
- `backend/src/main/java/.../controller/PropertyController.java`
  - Added `FailedUploadService` dependency (constructor injection). `uploadTaggedMediaAsset` now calls `recordFailure` on `MediaUploadException` (in its own TX) and resolves existing failure records on success via idempotency key.
- `backend/src/main/java/.../exception/GlobalExceptionHandler.java`
  - Added `@ExceptionHandler(MediaUploadException.class)` → HTTP 502, safe message only. Diagnostic logged internally at WARN.

**Frontend — New files**
- `frontend-web/src/services/failedUploadService.ts`
  - `fetchUnresolved()`, `fetchUnresolvedCount()`, `dismiss(id)`, `retry(id, file?)`.
- `frontend-web/src/components/FailedUploadsPanel.tsx`
  - Admin panel: card per failure with reason, stage, filename, age, retry count, status badge. Per-card actions: Retry, Replace file (hidden file input), Open property, Dismiss. Empty state when all clear. Auto-refreshes after action.

**Frontend — Modified files**
- `frontend-web/src/components/MasterAdminDashboard.tsx`
  - Added `AlertTriangle` icon and `FailedUploadsPanel` import. Added `failedUploadsCount` state fetched on mount. Added `failed-uploads` nav item with dynamic badge count. Renders `<FailedUploadsPanel>` when tab is active.

**Tests — New files**
